{"currentMessages":[{"content":"开始本次 Recommendation 执行。","role":"user","timestamp":1788854400000},{"api":"openai-completions","content":[{"text":"I'll analyze the recommendation task. Let me review the material.\n\nThe user's interest is photography learning, focusing on actual shooting methods, imaging principles, and adjustments under different conditions. They don't care about equipment promotions or photographers' private lives.\n\nLooking at the reaction history, there's a clear pattern:\n- Liked: \"操作记录\" (operation records) type articles\n- Disliked: \"条件与原理\" (conditions and principles) type articles\n\nWait, let me re-examine. The user's interest says they care about \"实际拍摄方法、成像原理与不同条件下的调整\" (actual shooting methods, imaging principles, and adjustments under different conditions). But the reaction history shows:\n- Liked: 操作记录 (operation records) - 儿童抓拍操作记录, 夜景曝光操作记录, 室内白平衡操作记录, 微距景深操作记录\n- Disliked: 条件与原理 (conditions and principles) - 儿童抓拍条件与原理, 夜景曝光条件与原理, 室内白平衡条件与原理, 微距景深条件与原理\n\nSo the user consistently likes \"操作记录\" (operation records) and dislikes \"条件与原理\" (conditions and principles) articles.\n\nThe interest description is user-authored and mentions imaging principles, but the reaction history strongly shows preference for operation records over conditions/principles content. However, the interest description is an explicit requirement. Let me consider.\n\nActually, the interest description says \"关注实际拍摄方法、成像原理与不同条件下的调整\" - this mentions both actual shooting methods AND imaging principles. But the reaction history shows a clear dislike of \"条件与原理\" type content.\n\nThe preferences list is empty (revision 9, no preferences). So there are no explicit preference directions beyond the interest description.\n\nGiven the reaction history is the strongest signal here, I should prefer \"操作记录\" (operation records) type content which the user consistently liked, and avoid \"条件与原理\" type content which they consistently disliked.\n\nLet me identify the \"操作记录\"